## THE CI STEP THAT JUDGES THIS, AND ITS PASS PREDICATE (MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER at main `8f1204ce`; re-read at your clone and quote)
`.github/workflows/npm-audit.yml` (blob `61a6804d`, 51 lines, unchanged since the first half): triggers `push: branches: ['**']` and `pull_request`; job `audit-production-deps`; node `'24'`; `npm ci --no-audit --no-fund` (line 34); then lines 41-49: `set +e`; `npm audit --omit=dev --audit-level=moderate --json > audit.json`; `STATUS=$?`; `set -e`; on non-zero it prints `jq '.metadata.vulnerabilities, ...'` and `exit "$STATUS"`. **Pass predicate: the job passes if and only if `npm audit --omit=dev --audit-level=moderate` exits 0 on the committed lock.** This lane's headline predicate (P1) is exactly that: **exit 0 and `metadata.vulnerabilities` all zero at your head, exit 1 with `moderate 12` at the unmodified main (red-first)**; the branch's own push run of `npm-audit` is judged by the same job (read its log by GET after the push and quote `metadata.vulnerabilities`). **Branch protection (drafter, `rules/branches/main`):** `required_status_checks` is an EMPTY list (the audit is not a required check), `code_scanning` CodeQL `alerts_threshold errors` and `security_alerts_threshold high_or_higher`, `deletion`, `non_fast_forward`.
**The test chain's predicate:** `build.yml:83` `- name: Run tests (verify gate)`, `:84` `run: npm run verify -- --maxWorkers=2`; `scripts/verify-suite.sh` (blob `eb9731f5`) `:343` fails when measured tests or suites are BELOW the counts file (`-lt`), `:354` ABOVE (`-gt`), `:366` prints `VERDICT: PASS`. So CI passes only if the measured pair EQUALS `scripts/verify-expected-counts.json` (blob `bcc17555` at main `8f1204ce`: `tests` **5268**, `suites` **311**, `_updated` "2026-11-01T04:10:34.933Z"; the first half's 5267 became 5268 when the RD-912 test landed). If you add test files or cells you regenerate the file ONCE with `npm run verify -- --maxWorkers=2 --update-counts` (the file's own `_why`; the worker argument is mandatory) and assert only `tests`, `suites` and `_updated` changed. `build.yml` runs on `pull_request` to main and `push` to main only: a push of your branch runs NO hosted Build; it first runs when Tuesday opens the PR. Say that in STATUS.

