## BEHAVIOUR PINS (what the lane adds; characterisation first, mutants prove the cells can fail)
A pin is a test that passes at the unmodified main AND after the change with the SAME assertions (a characterisation row), written FIRST at main and run there; a red at main means the pin is wrong, fix the pin, never the product. New cells go in ONE new test file `__tests__/rd913-archiver-sqlite3-characterisation.test.js` (additions only; no existing test body is edited unless a STOP-listed change below is approved). Closed list as a PROPERTY first: each pin names a behaviour the PRODUCT depends on, at its real call site, with an expected value read from main's behaviour, not from the library's documentation; at least these; any other shape: prove it meets the property or STOP.
- **Archive (through `streamExport` into a collecting writable, decoded by `__tests__/helpers/zip-entries.js`):** the set of entry names for a seeded data directory (copy the fixture style of `rd791-export-store-links` / `rd638-export-always-ends`), including `manifest.json` and `audit_log.sqlite` when present; each entry's bytes equal its source file's bytes; `manifest.json` parses and lists the same files; the compression method of each entry (record 8 or 0 as main produces; do not assert a method main does not produce); the resolved `{ filesIncluded, totalBytes }` and that `totalBytes` equals the bytes the destination received; an `archive` error still rejects and ends the response (the existing RD-638 cell; run it, do not duplicate it); a missing optional file is skipped, not an error.
- **SQLite (through `backend/simpleDb.js` on a temp database):** every statement family above has a cell, at least: (S1) the `User_Name != ""` read at 669 skips empty and NULL names; (S2) the `datetime("now")` update at 781 sets `updated_at` to a parseable timestamp (assert shape, not the value); (S3) `lastID` after an insert and `changes` after an update and a delete; (S4) the `serialize` transaction at 619-654 commits all rows and a forced failure rolls back (the pre-state is restored); (S5) `prepare`/`stmt.run` at 193 inserts the row it was given; (S6) an invalid statement rejects with an error carrying `code` `SQLITE_ERROR`; (S7) `close` resolves and a second open of the same file reads the rows written; (S8) a record with a unicode name and a 10 000-character value round-trips equal. Print `select sqlite_version()` before and after as information, NEVER assert it.
- **Mutants (a PROPERTY: each reverts or removes exactly ONE thing on a saved original, restore by writing the saved copy, never `checkout --`; print PREDICTED before RECEIVED; run only the new file and the seven export suites):** NOOP (comment only: all green); MA1 the archive adapter drops one `archive.file` entry (an archive pin goes red); MA2 `manifest.json` appended with the wrong name (red); MS1 line 669's `!= ""` changed to `!= "x"` (S1 red); MS2 `COMMIT` removed at 644 (S4 red); MS3 `this.changes` replaced by a constant (S3 red). A mutant that does not redden its named cell: STOP naming the figures. **Say plainly which paths have NO coverage today (the census), and which of them your pins still do not reach.**

